---
/**
 * Starfield — the site background.
 *
 * One fixed, pointer-transparent <canvas> behind every page. All of the
 * behaviour (density, twinkle, cursor response, parallax, reduced-motion and
 * touch handling) lives in src/scripts/starfield.ts; this component only
 * provides the element, its paint order and its place in the load sequence.
 *
 * `data-load="fade"` means the sky is the first thing to arrive (0ms), before
 * the nav, the wordmark and the rest of the page — and, because animations.css
 * gates every hiding rule behind `html.js` + `prefers-reduced-motion:
 * no-preference`, the canvas is simply visible when either is unavailable.
 *
 * The sky is decorative: aria-hidden, nothing focusable. If the canvas cannot
 * be created the aurora and vignette layers still give the page its depth.
 */
---

<canvas class="starfield" data-starfield data-load="fade" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>

<style>
	.starfield {
		position: fixed;
		inset: 0;
		z-index: var(--z-stars);
		inline-size: 100%;
		block-size: 100%;
		pointer-events: none;
	}
</style>
